---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About | gazza.ltd"
  description="What gazza.ltd is, how the tools work and the terms of using them. Free calculators that show their working, with nothing uploaded and no sign-up needed."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'About' }]} />

    <h1>About gazza.ltd</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Free calculators and everyday tools, built to show their working.
    </p>

    <div class="logo-panel">
      <img class="logo" src="/logo-full.svg" width="780" height="760"
        alt="Gazza Utilities — a magpie's head above the word gazza" />
      <p class="logo-caption">
        The magpie is a collector. Not of shiny trinkets — that turns out to be
        folklore rather than fact — but of genuinely useful things, cached away
        and remembered for when they're needed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why a magpie</h2>
      <p>
        The bird has a reputation for stealing anything that glitters, and it's
        a good story. It just isn't true. When researchers at the University of
        Exeter tested it properly, offering both captive and wild magpies shiny
        objects alongside dull ones, the birds showed no particular interest in
        the shiny ones and were mostly wary of anything unfamiliar. The myth
        seems to survive because we notice the times a magpie picks up a ring
        and forget the far more numerous times it picks up a twig.
      </p>
      <p>
        What magpies genuinely do is cache. They hide food in scattered places
        and remember where they put it. They're also one of the very few
        species to recognise themselves in a mirror, which puts them in
        select company.
      </p>
      <p>
        That felt like the right emblem for this site: a collection of small,
        useful things, kept somewhere you can find them again. And a bird whose
        best-known trait falls apart the moment anyone checks — which is a
        decent argument for showing your working.
      </p>

      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        gazza.ltd is a growing collection of single-purpose calculators and
        utilities — mortgages and tax, word games, text tools, PDF tools, with
        more added over time. Every tool is free, requires no sign-up, and runs
        entirely in your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>How the tools work</h2>
      <p>
        Each calculator explains the method it uses underneath the tool itself,
        with a worked example using real numbers, so you can check a result
        rather than just trust it. The finance tools go further: the tax rates
        they use are listed with the official source they came from and the
        date they were last checked.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing you type is sent anywhere or stored. The PDF tools are the
        clearest case — your files are processed on your own device and never
        uploaded, which is not true of most online PDF services. See the
        <a href="/privacy-policy"> privacy policy</a> for the full detail.
      </p>

      <h2>Terms of use</h2>
      <p>
        The calculators on this site are provided for general informational
        purposes only. They are not financial, legal, medical or professional
        advice, and results should be treated as estimates rather than
        guarantees. Formulas and reference data such as tax bands are kept as
        accurate and current as we can manage, but you should verify anything
        you're relying on for an important decision with a qualified
        professional or an official source.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind. We aren't
        liable for decisions made using the figures these tools produce.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This site is supported by display advertising, which is what keeps
        every tool free to use. See the <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy
        policy</a> for how advertising cookies work and how to opt out of
        personalised ads.
      </p>

      <h2>Tell us what's wrong with it</h2>
      <p>
        If a calculator gives a figure you think is incorrect, that's worth
        knowing about — send the numbers you entered and what you expected, and
        it'll get checked against the source. The same goes for a tool that
        behaves oddly on your phone, or one you wish existed and doesn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:hello@gazza.ltd">hello@gazza.ltd</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
